#: ../../source/docs/common-connecting-sport-fport.rst:5
#: 7b1ab33480b7449ea203f7bd0fe0b947
msgid "Connecting to FrSky Sport and FPort"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-connecting-sport-fport.rst:7
#: 21d8fd04308241f0be933421aabcdf5a
msgid "Some FrSky receivers have the ability to relay telemetry data from the vehicle to the transmitter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-connecting-sport-fport.rst:9
#: 16ca0b4c40ae4772889e604e0efda466
msgid "This was done initially via their SPort capability. And later, via an additional new protocol called :ref:`FPort<common-Fport-receivers>` which also includes the RC data to the autopilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-connecting-sport-fport.rst:11
#: 89c7093f0aa0464b9b45ca75a618d306
msgid "In order to connect to these ports on the FrSky receiver, any UART on the autopilot (normally a \"TELEM\" port) is used. However, both SPort and FPort are bi-directional protocols and require signal inversion in both directions in order to interface to the autopilot's UART."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-connecting-sport-fport.rst:13
#: 45aea4a214f94a728399cec00b6adfa7
msgid "if Sport is being used to send telemetry, then RC data must still be sent to the autopilot via its RCin pin as PPM or SBus from the FrSky receiver. See :ref:`common-flight-controller-wiring`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-connecting-sport-fport.rst:15
#: 82befe75289044e2b7ee1c0640bc6134
msgid "If the autopilot uses an F7 or H7 processor, then this can be done by appropriately configuring the UART port on the autopilot. However, most F4 based autopilots do not have this capability and required inverters externally. A few F4 autopilots have these on the boards themselves and label the port \"FrSky Telem\", but most do not. Those require an added :ref:`bi-directional inverter <frsky_cables>` connected between the autopilot and the receiver's SPort or FPort."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-connecting-sport-fport.rst:17
#: 27471e7db0344c979dcd93ce138971e5
msgid "F4 autopilots with on-board inversion (Pixracer,MindPX V2) default to having the inversion on their ports designated for FRsky telem, only requiring that the TX and RX pins be tied together and connected to the Sport/Fport on the receiver and the appropriate ``SERIALx_PROTOCOL`` be set for that port."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-connecting-sport-fport.rst:19
#: e4eb29d66b3741b08afec90acb6b11e7
msgid "In addition, some FrSky receivers provide an optional pad with the SPort or FPort already \"inverted\", so no external inversion is required if that is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-connecting-sport-fport.rst:21
#: f9b242613e2a440287084a3bdbf5e8de
msgid "**The various connection configurations are shown below (FPort is used in the diagrams, but just substitute SPort for the FPort labels in the images when using SPort connections):**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-connecting-sport-fport.rst:24
#: 8950267e98c142ac8197c1548d6def5a
msgid "Connections"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-connecting-sport-fport.rst:30
#: fd7a0e80daea401cb97b38f9535eb7c2
msgid "Fport: ``SERIALx_PROTOCOL`` = 23"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-connecting-sport-fport.rst:31
#: a67d7aa39b6f42d982ef4592cd40f349
msgid "Sport: ``SERIALx_PROTOCOL`` = 10"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-connecting-sport-fport.rst:39
#: a1ae6bc493094811b5fd3afc28c43e69
msgid "Fport: ``SERIALx_PROTOCOL`` = 23, ``SERIALx_OPTIONS`` = 4 (Half Duplex)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-connecting-sport-fport.rst:40
#: 782339fffee34ae0b0fa5b4ea8e2a9b3
msgid "Sport: ``SERIALx_PROTOCOL`` = 10, ``SERIALx_OPTIONS`` = 4 (Half Duplex)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-connecting-sport-fport.rst:42
#: b68a21508926491aab19c42f2180b4e4
msgid "modifying the receiver to access the \"un-inverted\" signal may not have enough drive, and/or, require the setting of the UART TX pin's pull-up resistor. Try using ``SERIALx_OPTIONS`` = 132 in that case."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-connecting-sport-fport.rst:44
#: f53f85678b6a4a61917a0c0a44244909
msgid "getting an \"un-inverted\" SPort or FPort signal from some receivers by tapping an internal connection may not provide enough drive for reliable operation on some autopilots having protection resistors in series with their UART pins, even when enabling the pull-up resistor on the UART. Contact the autopilot OEM for possible workarounds or use an normal FPort signal and external bi-directional inverter as shown above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-connecting-sport-fport.rst:52
#: 3d6f84c319bd4a4382506aef175e6127
msgid "Fport: ``SERIALx_PROTOCOL`` = 23, ``SERIALx_OPTIONS`` = 7"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-connecting-sport-fport.rst:53
#: 7f272527adc34045b6c7a302013fdf80
msgid "Sport: ``SERIALx_PROTOCOL`` = 10, ``SERIALx_OPTIONS`` = 7 (invert TX/RX, Half Duplex)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-connecting-sport-fport.rst:57
#: a987f997125c494385ca9d6f966a4bd4
msgid "F7/H7 boards can have the FPort connected to the UARTs RX pin, instead of the TX pin as shown above, and use the UART's SWAP option. F4 boards do not have this SWAP capability See :ref:`common-Fport-receivers` for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-connecting-sport-fport.rst:59
#: de547e05a2964b44aca13905f91d7adb
msgid "some autopilots, like the Cube Orange autopilot, have level shifters on their UART pins used on their Telemetry ports. This requires a 10K pulldown resistor externally on the receiver's SPort signal to work properly."
msgstr ""

